#!/bin/sh
#
# Refuse to push 밥친구 anywhere except its own repository.
#
# On 2 August this folder and ../k-food-map both had `origin` pointing at
# github.com/rkdals0121/kfoodmap. 밥친구 was merged into that repo's master and
# pushed, and kfoodmap.vercel.app — a different, live app — started serving
# 밥친구 instead. Nothing was lost, but the other project's production URL was
# wrong for several hours.
#
# `origin` has been removed from this clone and master now tracks test/main, so
# a bare `git push` is already safe. This hook is the part that survives
# somebody re-adding a remote later, including me.
#
# Install once:
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# To push somewhere new on purpose, add its host below rather than deleting
# this file — the list is the record of where this app is allowed to go.

ALLOWED='rkdals0121/test'

remote_url="$2"

case "$remote_url" in
  *"$ALLOWED"*) exit 0 ;;
esac

cat >&2 <<EOF

  push refused: this is 밥친구, and "$remote_url" is not its repository.

  밥친구 belongs to      github.com/$ALLOWED   (branch main)
                          → test-umber-phi-78.vercel.app

  The K-Food Map app lives in ../k-food-map and owns
                          github.com/rkdals0121/kfoodmap
                          → kfoodmap.vercel.app

  Pushing 밥친구 to that second repository replaced a live app once already.
  If this push is genuinely intended, add the host to ALLOWED in
  .githooks/pre-push.

EOF
exit 1
